      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "The contested phrase in the 1616 Inquisition minute that, at the 1633 trial, was used to convict Galileo. Bellarmine\u2019s actual personal warning had been milder \u2014 Galileo could not \u201chold or defend\u201d heliocentrism as physical truth. The minute in the file added \u201cor teach in any way,\u201d a far stricter prohibition; the document was quite possibly irregular or unsigned, but Galileo could not credibly contest it."
